<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Foreign Legion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Foreign Legion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Foreign <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> is a branch of the French army founded in 1831 for foreign volunteers. It served in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> and in many other colonial campaigns, becoming one of the best-known military instruments of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-foreign-legion.jpg" alt="French Foreign Legion" width="277" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Infographie Képi blanc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grenade_legion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
